From 0bc08eb55b713b418eb238ef0999553fff099807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mattryznar <ryznarmat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:42:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] Iskra: /scheme/sys/vmm, VMs for userspace (hypervisor
 step 4)

Opening /scheme/sys/vmm (root) creates a VM with one SVM vCPU and nested paging.
pwrite/pread below 1 TiB access guest memory (pages allocated on first write);
offset 1<<48 reads/writes VmRegs; offset (1<<48)+4K runs until the next exit and
returns VmExit. The kernel intercepts interrupts, all I/O ports, all MSRs,
CPUID, HLT and SVM instructions. vCPU runs switch all guest GPRs and use
VMSAVE/VMLOAD so FS/GS/TR and syscall MSRs never leak between host and guest;
SVM is enabled per CPU on first use. Closing the handle frees the VM.
---
